## Deduplication Strategy

**Stage 1 — Exact dedup (SHA-256)**
Every file is hashed. If the hex digest already exists in `images.sha256`, the
file is skipped — even if renamed or moved.

**Stage 2 — Near-dedup (perceptual hash / pHash)**
A 64-bit DCT pHash is computed. If the Hamming distance to any existing pHash
is ≤ 8, the image is flagged `is_duplicate=1` and linked to the canonical via
`duplicate_of`. Near-duplicates are still ingested so you can review them in the
Browser panel.

Pillow is used for pHash when available; a pure-Python DCT fallback is included
so the pipeline works without any ML dependencies.

